  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 137 AM CDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nTemperatures remain stagnant next week with high pressure to our\nnorth advecting in cooler air from the gulf. Temps will remain\nabove normal but highs in the mid 90s should feel a little better\nthan highs in the low 100s. Rain chances remain low in the basin\nbut should be higher west of the Pecos River where the mountains\nwill enhance lift. Uncertainty remains late next week due models\nhaving difficulty resolving tropical systems in the eastern\nPacific and the high pressure to our north. \n\nHennig",
